usage: python -m kit [-h]
                     {prizes,doctor,plan,cost,fetch,verify,rowscore,auc,hpscore,overlap,collate,surfacefix,provenance,compute,ensemble,gate,layers,shuffle,run}
                     ...

Command line: python -m kit {prizes,doctor,plan,cost,fetch,verify,rowscore,auc
,hpscore,overlap,collate,surfacefix,ensemble,gate,layers,shuffle,provenance,co
mpute,run}.

positional arguments:
  {prizes,doctor,plan,cost,fetch,verify,rowscore,auc,hpscore,overlap,collate,surfacefix,provenance,compute,ensemble,gate,layers,shuffle,run}
    prizes              open prizes from the dated snapshot
    doctor              check GPU, disk, tools and villa paths
    plan                print a First Letters run plan for an eligible scroll
    cost                estimate run cost in USD
    fetch               mirror a public bucket prefix over HTTPS (no AWS CLI
                        needed)
    verify              compare two ink maps (e.g. CPU vs MPS) with a control
    rowscore            text-row periodicity triage score for ink maps
                        (Bullo27's method)
    auc                 pixel AUC of an ink map against a segment's published
                        labels
    hpscore             letter-scale score: 48 um high-passed correlation with
                        the labels (Scheirer)
    overlap             do two segments trace the same papyrus? mesh gaps and
                        label agreement
    collate             two traces of one sheet as two copies: do their ink
                        maps agree, against a control?
    surfacefix          experimental region flags and bounded, controlled
                        surface corrections
    provenance          who ran what, when, from which inputs: a record and
                        one digest
    compute             machine time per run, from provenance records
                        (GENChase-style ledger)
    ensemble            average several ink maps of one surface (mean, or rank
                        mean across models)
    gate                Gate A: rank readers on PHerc0841's three crops by the
                        roadmap's rule
    layers              export a surface-volume zarr to 00.tif, 01.tif, ...
                        (v8in's input)
    shuffle             depth-shuffle control: copy a surface volume with its
                        layers in a fixed random order
    run                 local experiment ledger (experiments/, gitignored)

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
